# Scroll Substrate

Decisions: `docs/overhaul/EXPERIENCE_DECISIONS.md` (`X#`), `docs/overhaul/PLATFORM_DECISIONS.md` (`P#`); the as-built delta lives in `docs/SYSTEM_TRUTH.md`. Contracts win on conflict; fix this rule in the same PR.

## Hard constraints (break-if-violated)

- `JarvisRoot` (in `app/layout.tsx`) owns the only WebGL context for the tab. Never open a second `getContext("webgl" | "webgl2")` on `/`.
- Lenis + the scroll director own page scroll. Components never install their own `scroll` / `wheel` listeners, and never call `window.scrollTo` or `scrollIntoView`.
- Tailwind z-tokens only (`z-backdrop`, `z-substrate`, `z-content`, `z-decor`, `z-chrome`, `z-modal`, `z-toast`, `z-landing`). No raw `z-index`. No `position: fixed` outside L3 chrome.

## Features (new plugin work)

- New *product features* exposed as plugins live in `frontend/src/features/<id>/` + `backend/app/features/<id>/`, import via `@/sdk` only, and register in `features/index.ts`. Scaffold with `npm run new:feature <id>`. See `docs/overhaul/PLATFORM_DECISIONS.md` for SDK shapes.
- Evolving the desk itself — sections, chrome, FSM, scroll engine, substrate — goes directly in `core/` / `substrate/` and follows the contracts in `EXPERIENCE_DECISIONS.md` (`X#`) / `PLATFORM_DECISIONS.md` (`P#`). Do not stuff desk changes into a feature folder to bypass review.

## Hard don'ts

- Second WebGL context, feature-owned `requestAnimationFrame` loops, feature scroll/wheel listeners
- Inventing prices, rates, or dimensions with no tool/master-data source
- External/destructive acts without HITL Authorize (mail, calendar write, quote send, sheet write)
- Treating a parked approval as authorized
